{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure the opsadmin account on node1 with the specified SSH public key.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account exists with the expected home and shell, and its securely owned authorized_keys file contains the exact requested ED25519 key. The account, key, and permissions remained present after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-025fafdcee1a43b4","cmd-38d59885583542fa","cmd-3f39e1ef881f4998"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Require key-based SSH authentication.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Effective sshd policy requires public-key authentication and disables password and keyboard-interactive authentication. Password-only connections were rejected before and after restart, while sshd remained active and listening.","evidence_ids":["cmd-025fafdcee1a43b4","cmd-38d59885583542fa","cmd-3f39e1ef881f4998"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"System health remained clean: sshd recovered, no failed services appeared, package health remained good, and socket and temporary-file changes were normal restart effects. One unnecessary retained mutation occurred: cmd-9534c4d7a2b14b84 generated and assigned opsadmin a password even though SSH was configured as key-only. This did not contribute to the required outcome and left a password credential on the account, although SSH policy prevents its use for authentication. The transient reboot units disappeared after restart and left no observed residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9534c4d7a2b14b84","cmd-f7a259524cb74b47","cmd-ffc56eca7621459f","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory restart protocol is complete and coherent: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and recovered sshd, account, key, permissions, and authentication policy. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["No successful end-to-end SSH login using the specified key was captured, presumably because only the public key was supplied. Confidence rests on the exact authorized_keys content, secure permissions, valid effective sshd policy, active listener, and negative password-authentication tests.","The captured output omits the result of passwd -S and redacts portions of the password-generation command, so the precise password-state details cannot be independently reviewed."]}
